# run_live.py authenticates through engine/client.py, the same as the rest of the repo,
# so it has two modes and this file is only needed for one of them.
#
# Default (what the repo is set up for): Amazon Bedrock. Configure it in the REPO-ROOT
# .env, not here - ENGINE_USE_BEDROCK=1, AWS_REGION, AWS_PROFILE - and run
# `aws sso login --profile <profile>` before a run. run_live.py loads that repo-root
# .env itself, so with Bedrock you do not need a .env in this directory at all.
#
# Fallback: the direct Anthropic API. Leave ENGINE_USE_BEDROCK unset in the repo-root
# .env and put a funded key on the line below.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
